<title>SINGAPORE: Malayan Credit 1996 net up 14 percent.</title>
<headline>Malayan Credit 1996 net up 14 percent.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				50.7 vs   44.3</p>
<p>    Dividend (cents)			 6.0 vs    6.0</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     13.7 vs   12.2</p>
<p>    Turnover				 144.3 vs  136.8</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)		     3.8 vs    5.4</p>
<p>    Associates (group's share)	  41.2 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Share of results of associates    17.3 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Operating Profit			49.2 vs   57.5</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  70.3 vs   62.9</p>
<p>    Tax					 19.3 vs   18.0</p>
<p>    Minorities (losses)		    0.3 vs    0.6</p>
<p>Dividend pay date: May 26, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Malayan Credit Ltd is a property development company.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
